{"id":"uluru","name":"Uluru","qid":"Q33910","country":"Australia","locality":"Northern Territory","lat":"-25.345","lon":"131.036111111","built":"","year":null,"year_text":"","century":"","era":"Natural formations","period":"Neoproterozoic","date_basis":"","style":"","heritage":"","type":"inselberg","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uluru","text":"Uluru (; Pitjantjatjara: Uluṟu [ˈʊlʊɻʊ]), also known as Ayers Rock ( AIRS) and officially gazetted as Uluru / Ayers Rock, is a large sandstone monolith. It crops out near the centre of Australia in the southern part of the Northern Territory, 335 km (208 mi) south-west of Alice Springs. Uluru is sacred to the Pitjantjatjara, the Aboriginal people of the area, one of the groups collectively known as the Aṉangu.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uluru","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-9b3e17cc7cbc","w":1200,"h":786,"title":"Uluru, helicopter view, cropped.jpg","o":"gh-9b3e17cc7cbc.jpg","credit":{"text":"Corey Leopold","license":"CC BY 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uluru%2C_helicopter_view%2C_cropped.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-c27210fffe1c","w":1200,"h":900,"title":"Sunset at Uluru on July 30, 2005.jpg","o":"gh-c27210fffe1c.jpg","credit":{"text":"Thomas Schoch","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sunset_at_Uluru_on_July_30%2C_2005.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}}],"depictions":[{"id":"civilization-vi--uluru","game":"civilization-vi","name":"Uluru","verified":false,"text":"is a natural wonder in the Civilization games and the Aboriginal capital in the Call to Power games.","text_source":"https://civilization.fandom.com/wiki/Uluru","text_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","images":[{"id":"gh-p099a80acf12","w":186,"h":214,"o":"gh-p099a80acf12.png","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from Civilization VI, © 2K; As